<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 1500 CDT, boxed beef values were weak on fairly good demand and moderate to heavy offerings. Select and Choice chuck, round and loin cuts were weak, rib cuts generally steady. Beef trimmings were not established. -- USDA MArket News</p>
<p>391 Fab Lds   CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>    50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>56 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     103.88	103.19	 97.36	 96.64</p>
<p>		  -0.38	 -0.32	 -0.49	 -0.42</p>
<p>Rib	  158.25	156.77	148.61	148.54</p>
<p>Chuck	 70.69	 67.80	 70.08	 67.31</p>
<p>Round	 88.30	 88.30	 84.44	 84.44</p>
<p>Loin	 171.38	172.92	150.44	150.97</p>
<p>Brisket     58.06	 58.06	 58.09	 58.09</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  62.65	 62.58	 62.87	 62.71</p>
<p>Flank	 57.47	 57.47	 57.29	 57.29</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
